  "analyzed_vuln": {
    "function": "OT::hdmx::serialize",
    "file": "harfbuzz/src/hb-ot-hdmx-table.hh",
    "description": "In hdmx subsetting, OT::hdmx::serialize iterates source_hdmx->num_records and builds a DeviceRecord::SubsetView using source_hdmx->size_device_record, but it does not validate that each record is actually present/within the sanitized table bounds for that index. DeviceRecord::SubsetView::operator[] then computes widths[gid] from a potentially out-of-bounds source_device_record pointer and dereferences it in DeviceRecord::serialize (widths[i].set(*width)), causing a wild read crash (seen at BEInt<unsigned char,1>::operator unsigned char()).",
    "conditions": "Triggered via hb-subset-fuzzer on a malformed font containing an hdmx table with inconsistent metadata (num_records/size_device_record/table length). Data flow: harness loads attacker font -> hb_subset() -> _subset<const OT::hdmx>() -> OT::hdmx::subset/serialize. The crafted hdmx causes iteration over records that are not fully backed by input data; when subsetting glyph widths, code reads width bytes from invalid record memory, leading to ASan SEGV."
  },
